    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37061" root="كفأ" body-key="k">
    
      7 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انكفأ</span></b>  <i>He turned,</i> or <i>was turned, away,</i> or
<i>back,</i> from a thing that he desired to do; (S;)
[see also 1;] <i>he returned,</i> or <i>went back,</i> or
<i>reverted.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (TA,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَفَأَ</span></b> , (K,)
<i>It</i> (a party) <i>became routed, defeated,</i> or <i>put to
flight.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See 1, in two places.

